<GuiXml>
    <Animations>
        <!--
            Breathing pulse for the silence ring.

            Declared here rather than driven from Lua on purpose. The engine
            runs it, so there is no RegisterForUpdate and no per-frame Lua at
            all, which matters on console where the 1s-per-frame execution
            budget is shared across every installed addon, and which keeps
            faith with the 0.2.8 pass that removed per-tick work.

            playbackType/loopCount as XML attributes has precedent in ZOS's own
            compass.xml; the CreateTimelineFromVirtual instantiation in
            SilenceRing.lua is the idiom reticle.lua itself uses. Neither
            compass nor reticle is keyboard/gamepad split, so both are safe
            references for console behaviour.

            Applied to the Pulse texture only. The base Ring stays at constant
            alpha so the state never momentarily reads as "off": for a
            "you cannot cast" warning, a blink is worse than a glow.

            (Note for future editors: XML comments cannot contain a double
            hyphen, so the punctuation style here differs from the Lua files.)
        -->
        <AnimationTimeline name="UP_SilencePulse" playbackType="LOOP" loopCount="LOOP_INDEFINITELY">
            <Animations>
                <AlphaAnimation duration="350" startAlpha="0" endAlpha="0.9"/>
                <AlphaAnimation duration="350" delay="350" startAlpha="0.9" endAlpha="0"/>
            </Animations>
        </AnimationTimeline>
    </Animations>

    <Controls>
        <!--
            Silence ring.

            POSITION: GuiRoot CENTER with offsetY +108, which puts a 48px gap
            between screen centre and the ring's TOP EDGE.

            The offset is expressed as a control centre but the number that
            matters is the gap, so the two are related by half the ring's height:
            offsetY = gap + 60. Change the size and this has to be recomputed to
            hold the gap steady.

            History: +64 originally, i.e. the ring's CENTRE one reticle-height
            below the crosshair, which gave a 24px gap at the original 80x80
            size. Growing the ring to 120x120 shrank that gap to 4px without
            moving anything, since the extra radius came off the top. Respaced to
            a 48px gap on 2026-07-29.

            It is deliberately NOT anchored to the reticle, even though that
            would have worked:

              * ZO_ReticleContainer is declared AnchorFill (a full-screen
                container) and ZO_ReticleContainerReticle is anchored CENTER
                inside it with no relativeTo. The reticle's centre therefore IS
                screen centre, so this anchor is positionally identical while
                taking no dependency on a first-party control.
              * 64 is the reticle texture's height, fixed in ZOS's reticle.xml
                and never resized anywhere in reticle.lua.
              * reticle.lua hides the container and the reticle texture
                independently (stealth, disguise, several interaction states).
                A child control would inherit that and vanish while stealthed,
                including while silenced in stealth, which is exactly when this
                needs to be visible.

            SIZE: 120x120, raised from 80x80 (a 50% increase) on 2026-07-29.
            80 had matched the indicator tiles exactly; 120 is also a closer fit
            to the 256px source art, so there is less downscaling.

            No text anywhere in this control tree, so the gamepad-font trap
            documented in UI/Fonts.lua does not apply here.
        -->
        <TopLevelControl name="UP_SilenceRingRoot" mouseEnabled="false" movable="false" hidden="true">
            <Dimensions x="120" y="120"/>
            <Anchor point="CENTER" relativeTo="GuiRoot" relativePoint="CENTER" offsetX="0" offsetY="108"/>
            <Controls>
                <!-- Base ring: constant alpha, always the readable layer. -->
                <Texture name="$(parent)Ring" textureFile="UnderPressure/UI/Textures/silence_ring.dds">
                    <AnchorFill/>
                </Texture>
                <!-- Pulse overlay: alpha animated by UP_SilencePulse. Starts at
                     0 so it cannot flash at full opacity for one frame before
                     the timeline takes over. -->
                <Texture name="$(parent)Pulse" textureFile="UnderPressure/UI/Textures/silence_ring_pulse.dds" alpha="0">
                    <AnchorFill/>
                </Texture>
            </Controls>
        </TopLevelControl>
    </Controls>
</GuiXml>
